<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><description>Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 12:22:36 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category></category><title>Kenya shifts to electric cars as fuel prices soar 50%</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-kenya-shifts-to-electric-cars-as-fuel-prices-soar-50</link><description>
In Kenya, locally made eletric vehicles are gaining traction as fuel prices rise. As more and more Kenyans consider going electric, local firms are stepping up to assemble EV's domestically. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/801b0504-a6b7-11f1-b665-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1348699306a97f7b7ead947-66020292.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/801b0504-a6b7-11f1-b665-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-1348699306a97f7b7ead947-66020292.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">227b7832-a6b4-11f1-8fd4-97aa81b9fddf</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 11:19:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Illegal mining ravages Johannesburg neighbourhoods</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-illegal-mining-ravages-johannesburg-neighbourhoods</link><description>
Some houses in one Johannesburg neighbourhood are in danger of collapse because of illegal mining. Known as Zama Zamas, around 34,000 illegal miners are thought to be working in South Africa, in the hope of finding gold and chromium. The mines they dig hollow out the ground, which causes buildings to collapse as well as frequent power outages.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/979dd432-a6b6-11f1-8180-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-21356417506a97f631c90f48-96540535.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/979dd432-a6b6-11f1-8180-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-21356417506a97f631c90f48-96540535.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4b32d776-a6b3-11f1-9a33-97aa81b9fddf</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 11:14:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Iran: US accused of hitting wedding party in latest strikes</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-iran-us-accused-of-hitting-wedding-party-in-latest-strikes</link><description>
#Tehran says at least four people were killed and dozens more wounded in a #US strike on a town near in the south of #Iran, near the Strait of #Hormuz.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25c8019a-a6be-11f1-972d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-Iran-wedding.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25c8019a-a6be-11f1-972d-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-Iran-wedding.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">38fdb1b0-a6be-11f1-952b-d1be7233563a</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 11:11:30 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Military buildup seen in Ethiopia near Sudanese border</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-military-buildup-seen-in-ethiopia-near-sudanese-border</link><description>
A major military buildup has been observed on the Ethiopian side of the Sudanese border. It comes amid intensified fighting between the Sudanese armed forces and the Rapid Support Forces (RSF). Sudan and Ethiopia have both accused each other of supporting rebels within their borders.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f7430e9e-9170-11f1-ae5d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26105668493216.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f7430e9e-9170-11f1-ae5d-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26105668493216.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d1c0de36-a6af-11f1-bd07-97aa81b9fddf</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 10:57:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>FRANCE 24 in Nepal: In Bharatpur, authorities begin burying unidentified bodies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-france-24-in-nepal-in-bharatpur-authorities-begin-burying-unidentified-bodies</link><description>
In Nepal, the death toll continues to rise. Every day, new bodies are recovered, but many remain unidentifiable. Several days after the devastating floods, some are already in an advanced state of decomposition. Faced with the influx of remains, authorities have begun burying them without formal identification, primarily to limit health risks and the strong odours. FRANCE 24's special correspondents traveled to Bharatpur, in southern Nepal, to one of these burial sites.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7f1bfadc-a6b7-11f1-829a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/mini1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/7f1bfadc-a6b7-11f1-829a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/mini1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d25e53b6-a6b7-11f1-b43e-c7c8f9905ae8</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 10:28:09 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>Who is Trump's Venezuela go-between?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/press-review/20260902-who-is-trump-s-venezuela-go-between</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Wednesday, September 2: We look at papers' coverage of the shadowy Venezuelan magnate who brokered the Washington-Caracas oil deal. In other news, the Pacific Islands Forum wants to talk climate change, but China's anger at the presence of Taiwan is stealing the limelight. Finally, the Bayeux Tapestry is back in Britain after nearly a millennium, with perhaps some salacious secrets.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57065464-a6a5-11f1-9f63-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7051330296a97d93fefb3d2-98014263.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/57065464-a6a5-11f1-9f63-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7051330296a97d93fefb3d2-98014263.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">23d38552-a6a6-11f1-9ae5-2394582be977</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 10:22:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Antonia KERRIGAN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>450 applicants in a matter of seconds: The struggle to find rental flats in Paris</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-450-applicants-in-a-matter-of-seconds-the-struggle-to-find-rental-flats-in-paris</link><description>
September is the time of year when students in France are scrambling for accommodation, and this year, the available units are scarcer than ever. A whole series of factors, including tougher regulation of ecologically non-compliant apartments, means there are even fewer on the market.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f4f97600-a6b5-11f1-b1d5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-104302-104444-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f4f97600-a6b5-11f1-b1d5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-104302-104444-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f9c61bd4-a6b5-11f1-bef3-875c8e539070</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 10:12:17 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Hong Kong activist Joshua Wong could face life in prison after guilty plea</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-hong-kong-activist-joshua-wong-could-face-life-in-prison-after-guilty-plea</link><description>
Hong Kong pro-democracy activist Joshua Wong pleaded guilty to foreign collusion on Wednesday in a second national security trial against him that could see him jailed for life Elitsa Gadeva has more.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de214a3a-a6b4-11f1-a758-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-103730-103900-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/de214a3a-a6b4-11f1-a758-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-103730-103900-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e2d4ffea-a6b4-11f1-842c-97aa81b9fddf</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 10:11:14 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>What we know about alleged US strike on Iran wedding</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-what-we-know-about-alleged-us-strike-on-iran-wedding</link><description>
US forces launched fresh attacks on Iran Tuesday, including one that the Iranian Red Crescent said left four people dead at a wedding celebration, with Tehran vowing "severe punishment" for the strikes. France 24's correspondent in Tehran Reza Sayeh has the latest.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a2e90bb0-a6b4-11f1-b583-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-103152-103404-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a2e90bb0-a6b4-11f1-b583-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-103152-103404-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a79080ee-a6b4-11f1-a7fb-97aa81b9fddf</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 10:10:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>‘Tower of broken dreams’: French artist takes Eiffel Tower work to Burning man</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-tower-of-broken-dreams-french-artist-takes-eiffel-tower-work-to-burning-man</link><description>
A French artist from Saint-Malo-du-Bois in the Vendée region has taken a sculpture known as the “Broken Eiffel Tower” all the way to the United States. The 26-metric-ton structure was dismantled piece by piece to be shipped from the port of Le Havre before being reconstructed at the Burning Man festival in the Nevada desert. Caitlin Brown reports
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c5b12e0-a6b3-11f1-b78e-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-102513-102653-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c5b12e0-a6b3-11f1-b78e-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-102513-102653-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">917b0e10-a6b3-11f1-ba45-eb672b3e2093</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 10:08:11 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Hollywood in retreat as Venice Film Festival kicks off</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-hollywood-in-retreat-as-venice-film-festival-kicks-off</link><description>
The Venice Film Festival kicks off on Wednesday with the glamorous cinema showcase handing George Clooney a lifetime achievement award on its opening night. But despite the American star’s presence, this year’s festival features a distinct lack of films from Hollywood, reports France 24’s film critic Emma Jones.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/41c280e2-a6b3-11f1-8c40-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-102324-102437-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/41c280e2-a6b3-11f1-8c40-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-102324-102437-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4aa25354-a6b3-11f1-b9b2-97aa81b9fddf</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 10:05:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Why did Russia target Leipzig airport in alleged drone attack?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-why-did-russia-target-leipzig-airport-in-alleged-drone-attack</link><description>
The European Union and several individual member states have summoned Russian embassy officials over an attempted drone attack at Leipzig/Halle Airport last month, officials said on ‌Wednesday. Germany said on Tuesday it had concluded that ⁠Russia was responsible for the incident and ordered a series of measures, including the closure of a ‌consulate and a Russian cultural centre in Berlin. France 24's Andrew Hilliar takes a look at why Leipzig might be a target, and what the EU and Germany can do to prevent further incidents.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d4e805ce-a6b1-11f1-9d8a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-101340-101925-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d4e805ce-a6b1-11f1-9d8a-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-101340-101925-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d9ead330-a6b1-11f1-8454-eb672b3e2093</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 09:59:21 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Football: Senegal's Iliman Ndiaye signs with Manchester City</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20260902-football-senegal-s-iliman-ndiaye-signs-with-manchester-city</link><description>
Senegalese international Iliman Ndiaye has signed a contract with Manchester City that runs through 2031.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30925948-a67f-11f1-85b7-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/J24-ndiaye-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/30925948-a67f-11f1-85b7-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/J24-ndiaye-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9932a8ea-a67f-11f1-a000-7dc4763c3d39</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 09:51:24 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>L'Equipe TV</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>‘The sky is for drones’: Zelensky warns Russian skies unsafe for airlines</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-the-sky-is-for-drones-zelensky-warns-russian-skies-unsafe-for-airlines</link><description>
Ukraine's President Volodymyr Zelensky warned airlines and insurance companies on Tuesday that the presence of Ukrainian drones had made Russian skies dangerous to use and that they were effectively closed. "Today, we want to warn ‌every airline that uses Russian airspace, every insurer, everyone who still uses key Russian airports: ⁠the Russian sky is becoming completely dangerous," Zelensky said in his nightly video address.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c47bbe76-a6af-11f1-a499-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-101217-101338-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c47bbe76-a6af-11f1-a499-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-101217-101338-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c9315052-a6af-11f1-a60a-97aa81b9fddf</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 09:33:48 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Hong Kong activist Joshua Wong pleads guilty in second national security case</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-hong-kong-activist-joshua-wong-pleads-guilty-in-second-national-security-case</link><description>
Prominent Hong Kong pro-democracy activist Joshua Wong pleaded guilty Wednesday to conspiracy to collude with foreign forces to endanger national security under a Beijing-imposed law that has effectively stifled the city's once-thriving pro-democracy movement. France 24’s correspondent Jan Camezind Broomby says the decision will almost certainly mean more time behind bars for Wong, already serving a prison term of four years and eight months after entering a guilty plea in a separate national security case linked to an unofficial political primary.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a68246b2-a6ad-11f1-b6bc-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-100803-101142-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a68246b2-a6ad-11f1-b6bc-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-100803-101142-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ac23438c-a6ad-11f1-9f7d-414a38bed21c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 09:26:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Nepal floods: Families gather at overwhelmed morgues in desperate search for loved ones</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-nepal-floods-families-gather-at-overwhelmed-morgues-in-desperate-search-for-loved-ones</link><description>
In Nepal, the hope of finding survivors is fading daily. Bodies are piling up in morgues, and storage capacity is reaching its limit. Authorities are beginning to bury the remains after DNA samples are taken and an identification number is assigned. The hope is that families will be able to find them later. For the relatives of the missing, the wait is unbearable. They go from one hospital to another, consult the lists of survivors and scrutinise the photos of unidentified bodies. France 24's special correspondents met with several of these families at the morgue of Kathmandu University Hospital.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c24a1380-a6ac-11f1-94f5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-100540-100801-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c24a1380-a6ac-11f1-94f5-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-100540-100801-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c72d4da4-a6ac-11f1-a510-414a38bed21c</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 09:24:32 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Business</category><title>US energy secretary vows oil output will double on visit to Venezuela</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/business/20260902-us-energy-secretary-vows-oil-output-will-double-on-visit-to-venezuela</link><description>
US Energy Secretary Chris Wright landed in Venezuela on Tuesday ahead of a signing ceremony for a landmark oil deal between the US government and Venezuela. The deal would see the US create and control a private company that will hold 65 billion barrels in proven oil reserves. This agreement is also meant to encourage other US energy firms to invest in the country, in spite of serious challenges. In this edition, we see what other deals could be announced and what those challenges are.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5a13ef7c-a6a5-11f1-9ff6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7892170506a97d94538fc46-44037237.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5a13ef7c-a6a5-11f1-9ff6-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-7892170506a97d94538fc46-44037237.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3b69a350-a6a5-11f1-bcec-2550b3ae531d</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 09:17:57 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Charles PELLEGRIN</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Iran strikes back against latest US attacks, vowing ‘severe’ consequences</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260902-iran-strikes-back-against-latest-us-attacks-vowing-severe-consequences</link><description>
Iran struck US interests around the Middle East on Wednesday, vowing "severe" consequences for renewed American attacks on the Islamic republic, including a US strike it said killed five and wounded dozens of civilians at a wedding.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/783afdbe-a6ab-11f1-946a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-100213-100420-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/783afdbe-a6ab-11f1-946a-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260902-100213-100420-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7ccd5994-a6ab-11f1-962b-2394582be977</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 09:08:25 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Asia / Pacific</category><title>Nepal tunnel rescuers hit dead ends as search for trapped workers continues</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260902-nepal-tunnel-rescuers-hit-dead-ends-as-they-search-for-trapped-workers</link><description>
Rescue teams in Nepal were still searching Wednesday for hundreds of workers believed to have been trapped inside sprawling hydropower tunnels since the catastrophic flash flood that swept through the Himalayan region last week. Officials said that many of the tunnels remain totally blocked by mud and debris.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07368da2-a577-11f1-849f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/fe0cc43fd6df4a151e4418359eb746514777f1dd.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07368da2-a577-11f1-849f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/fe0cc43fd6df4a151e4418359eb746514777f1dd.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0a265e8e-a69e-11f1-b6d9-bbaab86a6a73</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 07:15:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/07368da2-a577-11f1-849f-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/fe0cc43fd6df4a151e4418359eb746514777f1dd.jpg">© Nepal Army handout via AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US Postal Service whistleblower warns new system could disrupt midterm election voting</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260902-us-postal-service-whistleblower-warns-new-system-could-disrupt-midterm-election-voting</link><description>
A US Postal Service whistleblower has warned that a new ballot-processing system ordered by President Donald Trump and due to launch Tuesday could prevent millions of Americans from receiving mail ballots ahead of November's midterm elections.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54d46668-a66e-11f1-b076-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20231662913911.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54d46668-a66e-11f1-b076-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20231662913911.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">18e0466e-a681-11f1-9fd8-dbb75d339c44</guid><pubDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 03:48:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/54d46668-a66e-11f1-b076-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP20231662913911.jpg">© Morry Gash, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Man accused of killing Charlie Kirk to face murder trial and possible death penalty</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260902-man-accused-of-killing-charlie-kirk-to-face-murder-trial-and-possible-death-penalty</link><description>
A judge in the US state of Utah has ruled that the man accused of shooting far-right activist Charlie Kirk will face trial for murder. Tyler James Robinson, 23, is accused of fatally shooting Kirk in the neck during a rally at a Utah college campus in September 2025, allegedly because he was 'fed up' with the 'hate' Kirk spread.
